course: dictionary
lesson: 8391
title: A rudder steers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rudder is a flat blade at the back of a boat or ship. When it turns left or right, the boat turns too, because the water pushes against the blade.
explain: Look at the clues in «The barge-woman steers with the tiller (the handle of the rudder).» Steers means guides which way something goes, and the tiller is the handle that turns the rudder. Ask: what word would fit here? Steering fits, so a rudder is the part that does the steering.
explain: On an aeroplane, the rudder is a flap on the tail, and it turns the nose left or right. Rudder can also mean something that keeps a person or plan on course, as in «without a rudder», which means with no direction in life.
fact: A rudder is a flat, upright blade at the back of a boat or ship.
fact: On an aeroplane, the rudder is a movable flap on the upright part of the tail.
fact: A barge is a long, flat boat on a canal, and it is steered with a tiller, the handle of the rudder.
fact: Labradors were bred to fetch from water, with a thick, waterproof coat and a thick, otter-like tail used as a rudder.
fact: «Without a rudder» is a phrase that means with no direction in life.
exercise: What is a rudder? | A sail that catches the wind | A rope that ties the boat to the harbour | *A flat blade at the back of a boat that steers it | A small anchor at the front of a ship
exercise: «The barge-woman steers with the tiller (the handle of the rudder).» What is the tiller? | The flat boat itself | *The handle that turns the rudder | The rope the horse pulls | The path beside the canal
exercise: On an aeroplane, where is the rudder? | *On the tail, as a movable flap | On the nose, as a window | In the cockpit, as a seat | Under the wings, as a wheel
test: «Without a rudder» in a story means what? | Floating in a swimming pool | Being full of happy friends | Having a very big, fast engine | *Having no direction in life
test: A story says, «The rudder broke in the storm.» What does this tell you about the boat? | Goes faster than before | Is ready for a race | Has been painted blue | *Cannot be steered and is in danger
exam: Which best describes a rudder? | A type of sea bird that lives on rocks | *A flat blade or flap that is turned to steer | A heavy anchor dropped to stop the boat | A tall mast that holds the sail up
